# Docs voice

Applies to sample guides under `docs/`, root `README.md`, and `src/**/README.md`
in this Contrib.Samples repository. These pages are not DocFX product docs.

## Zinsser

Strip every sentence. Cut words that do no work. Prefer short words and short
sentences. One idea when you can. Active verbs. Concrete nouns. No throat-clearing
and no decoration.

## Punctuation

No en dash (U+2013) and no em dash (U+2014). Use a period, comma, colon, or
parentheses. ASCII hyphen-minus only in compounds (`user-facing`) and in code.

## Lead and honesty

Lead with what is true and what to do. Do not open a page or section with a
negation. Contrast only when it adds information.

Sample READMEs state only what the code does. Be honest about stores:
**InMemory** and **SQL Server** only in this repo. Do not claim Redis, Postgres,
Azure Service Bus, or Wolverine. Do not claim a store or transport this sample
does not run.

## Banned voice

No ticket ids, plan-voice phrases, or "Historical. Do not rename."
Do not invent competitor comparisons on sample pages.

## What stays

"Do not" is for a footgun the reader will hit. Operational limits stay when the
next sentence is the action.

## Samples and code

Code in this sample is authority for what the sample does. Types and APIs come
from published LawnDart packages. Confirm package behavior against
sellistixorg/LawnDart at the package-matching tag when needed.

```markdown
<!-- BAD -->
Do not look for those knobs. They do not exist.

<!-- GOOD -->
Snapshots are one row per stream. A write replaces that row.
```
